# MANIFEST — the allowlist of record.
#
# Every file riprap installs into a project is named here. Nothing is copied
# because it happens to sit in the payload; the installer reads THIS file and
# refuses anything not listed.
#
# That is deliberate. A recursive copy will happily carry a .pyc, a .DS_Store, or
# an editor backup into someone else's public repo — and a compiled artifact
# embeds absolute source paths and identifiers that no text scrubber can see
# inside.
#
# Two tiers:
#   namespaced  riprap owns it. Overwritten wholesale on every install, and
#               pruned when upstream stops shipping it. Always under
#               bin/hooks/riprap/ or bin/riprap, so it can never collide with
#               anything the project already had.
#   seed        the project's own from the moment it lands; never overwritten.
#
# Generated by bin/build-manifest. Do not hand-edit — CI checks it matches the
# tree, and a hand-edit that drifts fails in whichever direction you did not test.
#
# Format: tier<TAB>path

seed	bin/format
seed	bin/hooks/git/pre-commit
seed	bin/hooks/git/pre-push
namespaced	bin/hooks/riprap/LICENSE
namespaced	bin/hooks/riprap/claude/block-destructive-outside-cwd.sh
namespaced	bin/hooks/riprap/claude/block-unreviewed-merge.sh
namespaced	bin/hooks/riprap/claude/format-on-write.sh
